# Metadata for one case study. This is sourced as a bash file, so quote
# any value containing spaces.
#
# Required:
TITLE="Nexora Technologies"
CLIENT_NAME="Nexora Technologies LLC"
PROJECT_URL="https://nexorany.com"

# The theme uses post_excerpt as the meta description AND as the card text
# on /portfolio/. Leaving it unset is what made this one's card run long:
# WordPress built its own from the body, ran the opening paragraph into
# the next heading, and cut it off with an ellipsis. Every other case
# study has one written for it.
EXCERPT="A development company's own site, built from nothing, then audited: five fixes took render-blocking to zero and accessibility to 100."

# Optional: up to 4 stats shown as the stat row on the case study page.
# A stat only gets set if both its NUMBER and LABEL are present.
#
# Mobile performance is quoted at its FLOOR, not its best. Across three
# sittings it came back 91, then 89, then 88. On 23 September five
# consecutive calls all returned 88 with a Speed Index identical to two
# decimal places - that is one cached result served five times, not five
# runs, so it is one data point and not four more.
#
# 88 is the lowest of everything seen and the figure PSI is currently
# handing out, so anyone who checks the site gets the number that is on
# the page. Quoting the 91 would have been the cherry-pick.
#
# Best practices (100) is the one left out, because showing both
# performance figures says more than a fourth hundred does. It is still
# in the body text.
STAT1_NUMBER="88"
STAT1_LABEL="Performance (mobile)"
STAT2_NUMBER="99"
STAT2_LABEL="Performance (desktop)"
STAT3_NUMBER="100"
STAT3_LABEL="Accessibility"
STAT4_NUMBER="100"
STAT4_LABEL="SEO"

# Optional: exactly one of these two for the featured image.
# FEATURED_IMAGE points to a local file, relative to this directory,
# that gets uploaded and attached. FEATURED_IMAGE_ID instead reuses an
# image already in the media library by attachment ID.
FEATURED_IMAGE="nexora-home.jpg"
# FEATURED_IMAGE_ID="123"
